{"id":"word:hebrew:H3162","type":"word","title":"יַחַד","subtitle":"H3162 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, a unit , i.e. (adverb) unitedly","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to יַחַד (H3162) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 142 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"יַחַד (yachad) means properly, a unit , i.e. (adverb) unitedly First listed occurrence: 1Chr 10 6."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"יַחַד","transliteration":"yachad","pronunciation":"yakh'-ad","strong":"H3162","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3162","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["יַחְדָּ֑ו","יַחְדָּֽו","יַחְדָּ֖ו","יַחְדָּ֔ו","יָֽחַד"],"morphs":[["HD",123],["HNcmsa",14],["HC/D",4],["HR/Ncmsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, a unit , i.e. (adverb) unitedly","usage":"alike, at all (once), both, likewise, only, (al-) together, withal.","full":"H3162. yachad יַ֫חַד 45 noun [masculine] unitedness . 1 as substantive only 1Chr 12:17 (peculiar) לֳי֑חַד לֵבָב עֲלֵיכֶֹם יִהְיֶהלִּֿי I will have a heart toward you for unitedness , i.e. my heart shall be ready to become one with yours (compare v. 12:38 אחד לב ). 2 elsewhere always in accusative as adverb in union, together (compare Arabic in accusative with suffix in his solitariness = alone ) — a. together , of community in action, place, or time (often combined, but one usually more prominent than the others); (1) in action, Job 38:7 אֵל כּוֺכְבֵי בְּרָןיַֿחַד when the stars of God shouted together ; Ezra 4:3 we together will build (opposed to you ), with נִלְחַם 1Sam 17:10 , נִשְׁמַּט Isa 43:26 ; (2) in place 1Sam 11:11 יָ֑חַד שׁנים בם נשׁארו ולא ; 2Sam 10:15 יָחַ֑ד וַיֵּאָֽסְפוּ Psa 2:2 ; 31:14 ; 88:18 Psalm 1 יַחַד שֶׁבֶת Isa 50:8 , as predicate Micah 2:12 אֲשִׂימֶנּוּ יַחַד ; (3) in place and time at once. 2Sam 21:9 יָ֑חַד וַיִּמְּלוּ and they perished together , 14:16 to destroy יחד בני ואת אתי ; (4) of time alone (poetry) Isa 42:14 יחד וְאֶשְׁאַף אֶשֹּׁם I will gasp and pant together , 45:8 ; Job 6:2 ; 17:16 **read נֵחָ֑ת for יַחַ֑ת ; יַחַד here will then belong to (1).; Psa 141:10 אעבור עד אנכי יחד while I at the same time pass on. b. all together, altogether (poetic synonym of כֻּלָּם but more forcible, suggesting often, especially with כל , all at once , as well as altogether ), Isa 44:11 יחד יבשׁו יפחדו (compare Psa 40:15 ), 62:10 יַחַד מֵהֶבֶל הֵמָּה they are all together (made) of vanity, Isa 22:3 יחד נדדו קציניך כל (with כל also Psa 41:8 ; Job 34:15 ): often in poetry beginning a clause with emphasis, Deut 33:5 ; Job 3:18 שׁאננו אסירים יחד 16:10 ; 19:12 גדודיו יבאו יחד , 24:4 ; 31:38 ; Psa 41:8 ; 98:8 ; Hosea 11:7 (with a negative), 11:8 ; in connection with a suffix, or object of a verb, Isa 27:4 יָ֑חַד אציתנה I will burn it altogether , Psa 33:15 לִבָּם יַחַד הַיֹּצֵר who formeth the hearts of them all together , 74:6 ; 74:8 ; Job 10:8 סָבִיב יַחַד altogether round about (but read perhaps with ᵑ6 ᵐ5 Del Di תִסּוֺב אַחַר ), 40:13 . c. together , in the sense of alike , the one as well as the other, Psa 49:3 ; 49:11 יאבדו ובער כסיל יחד Job 21:26 ; 34:29 . More frequent is יַחְדָּו 92 ( Jer 46:12 , 21 ; 49:3 יַחְדָּיו ), adverb together (properly (in) his or its unitednesses (compare Arabic alone ; and for the form אַשְׁרָיו ), but, the origin of the term. being forgotten, applied Generally as an adverb, without regard to number, Gender, or person: so Ges Ol § 135c Sta § 370a ) — together: a. of community in action , Psa 34:4 יחדו שׁמו ונרוממה let us exalt his name together , Isa 52:9 , with נוֺעַץ take counsel , 45:21 ; Psa 71:10 ; 83:6 ; Neh 6:7 ; נִצָּה to struggle Deut 25:11 ; in place, as with ישׁב Gen 13:6 ; Deut 25:5 , הלך Gen 22:6 , 8 ; Amos 3:3 , בוא Jer 3:18 ; Job 9:32 , קרב Isa 41:1 , נפל 2Sam 2:16 , אכל Judg 19:6 ; Jer 41:1 , התקבץ Josh 9:2 , נאסף Judg 6:33 , etc.; Deut 22:10 יחדו ובחמור בשׁור coupling pairs, and so strengthening וְ (mostly in poetry), 22:11 ; Amos 1:15 יחדו ושׂריו הוא (compare Jer 48:7 Qr [Kt יחד ], 49:3 ) 6:11-12 , י ונשׁים ׳שׂדות , 6:21 (accents), 13:14 ; 31:8 , 13 ; 50:4 , 33 ; Isa 41:19 , compare 65:7 ; in time (rare: but see below), Psalm 4:9 in peace ואישׁן אשׁכבה יחדו will I at once lie down and sleep (i.e. lie down and fall asleep immediately). b. emphatic (especially in poetry) = all together 1Sam 31:6 ; Isa 10:8 מלכים יחדו שׂרי הלא are not my princes all together , all alike, kings? 18:6 ; 40:5 ; 41:20 , 23 ; 45:16 (|| כֻּלָּם ), 46:2 יחדו כרעו קרסו , 48:13 ; 66:17 ; Psa 14:3 (|| הַכֹּל ), 19:10 יחדו צדקו (of J.'s ordinances), 35:26 ; 37:38 ; sometimes (like יַחַד b ) suggesting all at once , as well as all together , Exod 19:8 יחדו העם כל ויענו (so, with כל , Isa 22:3 ; 31:3 ; Zech 10:4 ), Isa 1:28 , 31 יחדו שׁניהם ובערו . Prefixed to a clause (like יחד ), Deut 33:17 (compare יחד 33:5 ), Isa 9:20 ; 11:7 , 14 ; 31:3 ; 43:17 ; 45:16 ; 52:8 ; Jer 46:12 ; 51:38 ; Lam 2:8 ; Job 24:17 (strengthening לָמוֺ ) c. alike , the one as well as the other, Deut 12:22 (= 15:22 ) the unclean and the clean alike may eat it, 1Sam 30:24 יַחֲלֹקוּ׃ יַחְדָּו they shall share together , i.e. alike.","rootNote":"from 3161 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 10 6","keyReferences":["1Chr 10 6","1Chr 12 18","1Kgs 3 18","1Sam 11 11","1Sam 17 10","1Sam 30 24","1Sam 31 6","2Sam 2 13"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":142,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 10 6","book":"1Chr","chapter":10,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יַחְדָּ֥ו","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"1Chr 12 18","book":"1Chr","chapter":12,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/יָ֑חַד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 3 18","book":"1Kgs","chapter":3,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יַחְדָּ֗ו","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"1Sam 11 11","book":"1Sam","chapter":11,"verse":11,"